Now we have all precursors.

Let's list the route hierarchy.

Root molecule target SMILES.

Children: first reaction (template 324324) with two children molecules: precursor A (acid) and precursor B (Nc1ccccc1N).

Precursor A further has reaction (template 1914396) with two children: precursor A1 (aryl aldehyde) and precursor A2 (O=C(O)CC(=O)O) (malonic acid? Actually O=C(O)CC(=O)O is succinic acid? It's oxalic? It's malonic acid). Then precursor A1 further has reaction (template 733) with two children: precursor A1a (Cc1ccc(N)cc1) (p-toluidine) and precursor A1b (O=Cc1ccc(S(=O)(=O)Cl)cc1) (aryl aldehyde with sulfonyl chloride). That completes three reactions.

We also have precursor B (Nc1ccccc1N) which is terminal (no further reactions). Also A2 is terminal.

Now we need to construct JSON.

Structure:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles": target,
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":324324,
     "children":[
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)O)cc2)cc1"},
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Nc1ccccc1N"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

But we need to embed further reactions under the first precursor. So the first precursor node should have its own children (reaction). So we need nested structure: the first precursor is a molecule node that has a child reaction.

Thus:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles": target,
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id":"324324",
     "children":[
        {
          "type":"mol",
          "smiles":"Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)O)cc2)cc1",
          "children":[
            {
              "type":"reaction",
              "template_id":"1914396",
              "children":[
                {
                  "type":"mol",
                  "smiles":"Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(C=O)cc2)cc1",
                  "children":[
                    {
                      "type":"reaction",
                      "template_id":"733",
                      "children":[
                        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Cc1ccc(N)cc1"},
                        {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=Cc1ccc(S(=O)(=O)Cl)cc1"}
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=C(O)CC(=O)O"}
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Nc1ccccc1N"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

Make sure template_id values are numbers or strings? Example earlier used number 1234. We'll use numbers without quotes.

Now final answer.
